[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains queries with a UML property as receiver.
This includes queries for retrieving property metadata
(multiplicity, cardinality), classifying properties as
attributes or association ends, and navigating to the
owning classifier or association.

Note: In UML, association ends are represented as
properties. Queries in this module handle both plain
attributes (association = null) and association ends
(association <> null). The distinction is made explicit
in the query documentation where relevant.

Note: Queries that find properties starting from a class
or data type are in classQuery and dataTypeQuery
respectively, since their receiver is the owning
classifier rather than the property itself.

Related modules:
- classQuery: queries with a UML class as receiver,
  including queries that find attributes and
  association ends of a class
- dataTypeQuery: queries with a UML data type as receiver,
  including queries that find attributes of a data type
- associationQuery: queries with a UML association as
  receiver, since association ends are properties
/]
[module propertyQuery(
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[**
Returns the cardinality of a property in ShEx syntax:
'?' for 0..1, '*' for 0..*, '+' for 1..*, '' for all other cases.
Note: the upper bound is an Integer; unlimited is represented as -1,
both in the UML metamodel and at runtime (regardless of the XMI
serialization which can use the asterisk).

@param aProperty - A UML property whose multiplicity is to be
                   expressed as a ShEx cardinality string.
/]
[query public u_shexCardinality(
  aProperty : uml::Property) : String =
  if aProperty.lower = 0 and aProperty.upper = 1 then
    '?'
  else if aProperty.lower = 0 and aProperty.upper = -1 then
    '*'
  else if aProperty.lower = 1 and aProperty.upper = -1 then
    '+'
  else
    ''
  endif
  endif
  endif
/]

[**
Returns the multiplicity of the specified property as a string
in the format "lower..upper", e.g. "0..1", "1..*".

@param aProperty - A UML property whose multiplicity is to be
                   retrieved.
/]
[query public u_docMultiplicity(
  aProperty : uml::Property) : String =
  aProperty.lower.toString() + '..' + aProperty.upper.toString()
/]
